{
  "_comment": "SYNTHETIC drift cases. Every label and harm value is AUTHOR-ASSIGNED using the rubric below, not observed in a real incident. One drifted attribute per case; the renderer expands each into a Terraform plan (terraform show -json, format 1.2), CloudTrail records and an ITSM ticket export.",
  "rubric": {
    "0": "best outcome; nothing lost",
    "1": "toil: a reviewer spends time; nothing is exposed or broken while they look (the floor for HUMAN_REVIEW)",
    "2": "debt: IaC and live disagree for longer, an intended benign change is lost and must be redone, or a temporary fix is made permanent before review",
    "3-4": "moderate: tier-2/3 redundancy loss, a low/medium policy violation persists, an unreviewed change to a sensitive resource is legitimised, or exposure during hours of review",
    "5-6": "serious: tier-1 redundancy loss, a medium-high violation persists, a suspicious change is hidden, or a planned migration is rolled back",
    "7-8": "severe: a high-severity exposure persists for days, or a tier-1 service loses capacity it needs",
    "9-10": "critical: world-open data or admin access persisted, or an active tier-1 incident is re-triggered"
  },
  "actions": {
    "REVERT": "terraform apply: live goes back to the IaC value",
    "CODIFY": "open a PR that changes IaC to the live value",
    "QUARANTINE": "keep live, suppress automated reconciliation of this attribute (ignore_changes or a drift hold with an expiry), no code change yet",
    "HUMAN_REVIEW": "change nothing, page the owning team with the evidence"
  },
